istry.npmjs.org","port":443,"connections":15,"sent":92848,"received":32365387}],"blocked":[{"host":"antigravity-unleash.goog","port":443,"connections":2,"reason":"antigravity-unleash.goog isn't in the allowlist"},{"host":"play.googleapis.com","port":443,"connections":10,"reason":"play.googleapis.com isn't in the allowlist"}]},"outcome":"pass","error":null,"durationMs":49812,"turns":[{"prompt":"ES (Eval Suite) is an eval runner for coding agents: npm package @invertase/foobar, CLI `es`. This version isn't on the npm registry: install it from the tarball /opt/es/invertase-foobar.tgz. There's no Docker and no API key in here, so use ES's fake harness, fake sandbox and fake judge. This folder is empty. Set up ES here: an es.config.ts and one eval in evals/hello.es.ts that asks the agent to create hello.txt containing \"hello\" and checks that file with a deterministic assertion. Finish when `npx es run` passes.","status":"completed","startedAt":"2026-09-26T14:12:42.865Z","durationMs":43853,"text":"ES has been set up with the fake harness, fake sandbox, and fake judge.\n\n### Summary of Actions Taken\n\n1. **Installed `@invertase/foobar`**: Initialized [`package.json`](file:///es/workspace/package.json) and installed `@invertase/foobar` from `/opt/es/invertase-foobar.tgz`.\n2. **Configured ES**: Created [`es.config.ts`](file:///es/workspace/es.config.ts) utilizing `fakeHarness`, `fakeSandbox`, and `fakeJudge`:\n   ```ts\n   import { defineConfig } from '@invertase/foobar'\n   import { fakeHarness } from '@invertase/foobar/harness'\n   import { fakeJudge } from '@invertase/foobar/judge'\n   import { fakeSandbox } from '@invertase/foobar/sandbox'\n\n   export default defineConfig({\n     harness: fakeHarness({ files: { 'hello.txt': 'hello\\n' }, text: 'Created hello.txt.' }),\n     sandbox: fakeSandbox(),\n     judge: { model: fakeJudge({ score: 0.9 }) },\n   })\n   ```\n3. **Created Eval**: Added [`evals/hello.es.ts`](file:///es/workspace/evals/hello.es.ts) with deterministic assertion on the created file:\n   ```ts\n   import { evaluate, expect, group } from '@invertase/foobar'\n\n   group('hello', () => {\n     evaluate('creates hello.txt', async (t) => {\n       const turn = await t.send('Create hello.txt containing \"hello\".')\n       await expect(turn).toHaveFile('hello.txt', /hello/)\n     })\n   })\n   ```\n4. **Verified**: Executed `npx es run`, passing the eval attempt in 62ms with exit code 0.\n"}],"timings":{"setupMs":1994,"agentMs":43854,"diffMs":95,"checksMs":2171,"judgeMs":1324},"activity":{"tools":17,"fileEdits":4,"webSearches":0,"webFetches":0,"reasoningMs":0},"judgements":[{"verdict":"pass","score":1,"threshold":0.8,"question":"Pass only if the eval sends the agent a task with t.send, checks hello.txt with a deterministic assertion (for example toHaveFile, t.readFile with expect, or t.exec), and the config uses a fake harness that writes hello.txt, with the fake sandbox.","model":"google/gemini-3.8-flash","resolvedModel":"gemini-3.8-flash","key":"0:4a2edaacd1d8"}],"checks":[{"command":"npx --no-install es run --dry-run --json","exitCode":0,"durationMs":908,"log":{"path":"evals-scaffold-es-ts-from-scratch-scaffolds-a-first-eval-and-fca4bd/antigravity-gemini-3-8-flash-low-es-good-es-tarball-b63f69/1/checks/1.log","sha256":"3b39c89a6186c673069819266e84c885acb5eab4ad9a07edb140854e617688c8","bytes":1345}},{"command":"grep -rq \"hello.txt\" evals","exitCode":0,"durationMs":45,"log":{"path":"evals-scaffold-es-ts-from-scratch-scaffolds-a-first-eval-and-fca4bd/antigravity-gemini-3-8-flash-low-es-good-es-tarball-b63f69/1/checks/2.log","sha256":"ed15ce03dc64516b8e8779d1678f3a5d52cde9b7b53cf38bc3bd6764e829db83","bytes":58}},{"command":"npx --no-install es run --ui plain","exitCode":0,"durationMs":1218,"log":{"path":"evals-scaffold-es-ts-from-scratch-scaffolds-a-first-eval-and-fca4bd/antigravity-gemini-3-8-flash-low-es-good-es-tarball-b63f69/1/checks/3.log","sha256":"ce1bcff32299a36a639f0cdd185ed0fdfb7a9723e964a4ed0bb9311886db6